 (step 1): Configure Jenkins Pipeline

Create New Pipeline Job
Open Jenkins dashboard and click "New Item"

Enter job name: pkc-chief-pipeline

Select "Pipeline" and click "OK"

In the configuration page:

Check "GitHub project" and add repository URL

Under "Build Triggers", check "GitHub hook trigger for GITScm polling"

Under "Pipeline" section:

Definition: "Pipeline script from SCM"

SCM: "Git"

Repository URL: https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/pkc-chief.git

Branch: */main

Script Path: Jenkinsfile

Add Docker Hub Credentials
Go to "Manage Jenkins" → "Manage Credentials"

Click "Global" → "Add Credentials"

Configure:

Kind: "Username with password"

Username: pkc0812 (your Docker Hub username)

Password: Your Docker Hub password/token

ID: dockerhub-credentials

(Step 2): Configure GitHub Webhook

Set Up Webhook in GitHub
Navigate to your GitHub repository pkc-chief

Go to "Settings" → "Webhooks"

Click "Add webhook"

Configure webhook:

Payload URL: http://YOUR_JENKINS_IP:8080/github-webhook/

Content type: application/json

Secret: Leave empty (or add Jenkins API token for security)

Which events: Select "Just the push event"

Active: Checked

Jenkins pipeline script Groovy:-

pipeline {
    agent any
    
    environment {
        DOCKER_IMAGE = "pkc0812/jenkins-ci-cd-webhook"
        DOCKERHUB_CREDENTIALS = 'dockerhub_jenkins'
        GITHUB_CREDENTIALS = 'github_jenkins'
    }
    
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git branch: 'main', 
                    url: 'https://github.com/pkc0812/jenkins-ci-cd-webhook.git',
                    credentialsId: "${GITHUB_CREDENTIALS}"
            }
        }
        
        stage('Build Docker Image') {
            steps {
                script {
                    echo "Building Docker image: ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${BUILD_NUMBER}"
                    def dockerImage = docker.build("${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${BUILD_NUMBER}")
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Push to DockerHub') {
            steps {
                script {
                    docker.withRegistry('', DOCKERHUB_CREDENTIALS) {
                        def dockerImage = docker.image("${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${BUILD_NUMBER}")
                        dockerImage.push()
                        dockerImage.push("latest")
                        echo "Successfully pushed ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${BUILD_NUMBER} and latest to DockerHub"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Clean Local Images') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // Clean up local images except the latest ones
                    sh """
                        echo "Cleaning up local Docker images..."
                        docker image prune -f --filter "until=24h"
                    """
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Deploy Container') {
            steps {
                script {
                    // Stop and remove existing container if running
                    sh '''
                        echo "Stopping existing container..."
                        docker stop jenkins-webhook-app || true
                        docker rm jenkins-webhook-app || true
                    '''
                    
                    // Deploy new container
                    sh """
                        echo "Deploying new container..."
                        docker run -d \
                        --name jenkins-webhook-app \
                        -p 8082:80 \
                        ${DOCKER_IMAGE}:${BUILD_NUMBER}
                    """
                }
            }
        }
        
        stage('Health Check') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sleep(10) // Wait for container to start
                    sh """
                        echo "Performing health check..."
                        curl -f http://localhost:8082 || exit 1
                        echo "Application is running successfully!"
                    """
                }
            }
        }
    }
    
    post {
        always {
            echo "Pipeline execution completed!"
            sh "docker ps | grep jenkins-webhook-app || echo 'Container not running'"
        }
        success {
            echo "✅ Pipeline executed successfully!"
            echo "🌐 Application available at: http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:8082"
        }
        failure {
            echo "❌ Pipeline failed!"
            // Cleanup on failure
            sh '''
                docker stop jenkins-webhook-app || true
                docker rm jenkins-webhook-app || true
            '''
        }
    }
}

